  {
    "id": "anno-ichinoseki_upper_p029_right-02",
    "type": "Annotation",
    "body": [
      {
        "purpose": "transcribing",
        "value": "込高新田高　壹萬三千三百四拾七石三斗七升"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "modern_jp_reading",
        "value": "込高・新田高 一万三千三百四十七石三斗七升／こみだか しんでんだか 13,347.37こく"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "english_translation",
        "value": "Incorporated yield together with newly reclaimed (shinden) field yield, as printed: 13,347.37 koku. The label is a two-line warichu — right line 込高新 (x2076-2127), left line 田高 (x2025-2072), read right line first. FLAG, cross-page arithmetic does not reconcile: the same 一關藩 return on the facing page (upper_p028_left, printed 31) gives 草高 三萬三百四拾七石三斗七升 = 30,347.37 and 高 二萬七千石 = 27,000, so 27,000 + 13,347.37 = 40,347.37, which exceeds the printed 草高 by exactly 10,000. Every glyph of this column was checked at 8x and the leading 壹 is unmistakable, and the column carries exactly fourteen value glyphs on a regular pitch, so this is not a misreading. Two explanations remain open: the print may carry a spurious 壹萬, since 30,347.37 − 27,000 = 3,347.37 reproduces the rest of this figure exactly; or the 27,000 is the shogunate-facing omotedaka rather than a component of the 草高, in which case 30,347.37 − 13,347.37 = 17,000 would be the base honden yield. The figure is recorded as printed and the discrepancy left open. MASTER carries 草高 30,347.37 for 一關藩 (with the note 高(omote) 二萬七千石) but no row for this field."
      },
      {
        "purpose": "identifying",
        "value": "込高新田高"
      }
    ],
    "target": {
      "source": "images/upper_p029_right.jpg",
      "selector": {
        "type": "FragmentSelector",
        "conformsTo": "http://www.w3.org/TR/media-frags/",
        "value": "xywh=pixel:2015,1241,122,1424"
      }
    }
  },
